  <section class="content-section reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-6">
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Operational scenarios</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Where smart building infrastructure delivers</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>Real estate developers across the MEA region face scenarios where building infrastructure quality directly determines tenant acquisition, retention, and operating cost. MEAICON's platforms address three use cases that define modern commercial real estate.</p>
          <p><strong>Smart building infrastructure designed during construction.</strong> Gulf property developers constructing premium commercial towers cannot afford to retrofit smart features after occupancy. MEAICON designs fibre backbone, structured wireless coverage, IoT sensor platforms, and building management system integration during construction planning — integrated with architectural drawings before concrete is poured. This avoids the cable runs, coverage gaps, and fragmented systems that plague retrofit projects.</p>
          <p><strong>Edge AI analytics for energy optimisation.</strong> Commercial towers in the Gulf face extreme cooling loads that drive energy costs. MEAICON deploys floor-level edge AI nodes that process sensor data locally — occupancy patterns, temperature trends, and air quality metrics — adjusting climate and lighting in real time without round-tripping to a central server. When zones are unoccupied, the system automatically reduces cooling and lighting, achieving significant energy cost reduction within months of operation.</p>
          <p><strong>Tenant digital experience from day one.</strong> Premium multinational tenants expect mobile access, climate preference setting, and meeting room booking as standard features. MEAICON delivers a tenant-facing digital experience layer that is functional from the first day of occupancy — not a post-handover add-on. The application integrates with building infrastructure through the same IoT platform that powers property management, avoiding the fragmented experience typical of retrofit smart buildings.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

